    "sections": {
        "description": "<p>appiapp Carousel Block is a flexible Gutenberg carousel for building responsive sliders directly in the block editor. Choose a standard content carousel, an image gallery, or a post carousel powered by Query Loop.</p>\n<p>Custom Content Carousel: Add any Gutenberg block, including text, images, buttons, and more.</p>\n<p>Image Gallery Carousel: Create elegant image sliders with lightbox support.</p>\n<p>Post Carousel: Automatically showcase your latest blog posts in a dynamic slider.</p>\n<p>Features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully integrated with Gutenberg</li>\n<li>Supports Embla Carousel, Swiper, and CSS-only modes</li>\n<li>Adjustable navigation with arrows, bullets, and progress bars</li>\n<li>Lightbox support for galleries</li>\n<li>Query Loop integration for post carousels</li>\n<li>Responsive item counts, spacing, and breakpoints</li>\n<li>Optional custom CSS and JavaScript controls</li>\n<li>A growing library of free, ready-to-customize templates</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Template Library</h3>\n<p>Choose from a growing collection of carousel templates directly in the block editor. Every template is included for free and is ready to customize.</p>\n<p>Templates that were previously presented as premium are now included for free. There are no premium-only templates, locked layouts, or paid upgrades. Open the Template Library from the carousel block or from the editor Command Palette and insert any available design without leaving the block editor.</p>\n<h3>External services</h3>\n<p>The Template Library retrieves its manifest, previews, and template content from the jsDelivr CDN (<code>cdn.jsdelivr.net</code>) when an authorized user opens or refreshes the library. Administrators can optionally enable a daily WP-Cron check for new and updated templates. Automatic checks are disabled until an administrator provides consent and can be disabled at any time from the Template Library.</p>\n<p>The plugin does not intentionally send WordPress content, user account details, or telemetry. Like any web request, jsDelivr receives standard connection data such as the site server IP address. See the <a href=\"https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">jsDelivr privacy policy</a>.</p>\n",
        "installation": "<p>Go to Plugins &gt; Add New in your WordPress dashboard.</p>\n<p>Search for &#8220;appiapp Carousel Block&#8221;.</p>\n<p>Click Install Now and then Activate.</p>\n<p>Add the &#8220;appiapp Carousel Block&#8221; block in Gutenberg and start building amazing sliders!</p>\n<p>Alternatively, you can upload the plugin manually:</p>\n<p>Download the ZIP file.</p>\n<p>Go to Plugins &gt; Add New &gt; Upload Plugin.</p>\n<p>Select the ZIP file, click Install Now, and then Activate.</p>\n",
        "faq": "\n<dt id=\"does%20it%20work%20with%20any%20theme%3F\">\nDoes it work with any theme?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>appiapp Carousel Block is built for Gutenberg and works with WordPress themes that support the block editor.</p>\n</p>\n<dt id=\"can%20i%20use%20my%20own%20custom%20styles%3F\">\nCan I use my own custom styles?\n</h4>\n<p>\n<p>Yes. You can customize colors, spacing, and layouts in the block editor or use additional CSS for advanced styling.</p>\n</p>\n\n",
        "changelog": "<h4>3.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Added the in-editor Template Library with free templates and previews</li>\n<li>Added access to the Template Library from the carousel placeholder and Command Palette</li>\n<li>Added optional automatic template update checks with explicit administrator consent</li>\n<li>Improved Swiper, Embla, CSS-only, gallery, lightbox, and Query Loop behavior</li>\n<li>Improved keyboard accessibility and responsive editor previews</li>\n<li>Hardened remote template validation, URL handling, and cache fallbacks</li>\n<li>Added automated browser coverage for WordPress 6.6 and current WordPress releases</li>\n<li>Removed legacy premium and upgrade references</li>\n<li>Improved performance, code quality, and WordPress.org compatibility</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>2.0.0</h4>\n<p>Major update – appiapp Carousel now includes advanced features! 🎉</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully responsive with customizable breakpoints  </li>\n<li>Multiple layout options, including vertical alignment  </li>\n<li>Adjustable navigation (arrows, bullets, progress bars)  </li>\n<li>Lightbox support for image galleries  </li>\n<li>Query Loop integration for post carousels  </li>\n<li>Direct Gutenberg integration – no shortcodes needed  </li>\n<li>Optimized performance and stability improvements  </li>\n</ul>\n<h4>1.0.0</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Initial release with full Gutenberg integration</li>\n<li>Supports Embla Carousel, Swiper JS, and CSS-only modes</li>\n<li>Initial release – enjoy building amazing carousels! 🚀</li>\n</ul>\n"
    },
    "short_description": "appiapp Carousel allows you to create highly customizable carousels directly in Gutenberg. Build unique sliders for posts, images, and any block.",
    "description": "<p>appiapp Carousel Block is a flexible Gutenberg carousel for building responsive sliders directly in the block editor. Choose a standard content carousel, an image gallery, or a post carousel powered by Query Loop.</p>\n<p>Custom Content Carousel: Add any Gutenberg block, including text, images, buttons, and more.</p>\n<p>Image Gallery Carousel: Create elegant image sliders with lightbox support.</p>\n<p>Post Carousel: Automatically showcase your latest blog posts in a dynamic slider.</p>\n<p>Features:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Fully integrated with Gutenberg</li>\n<li>Supports Embla Carousel, Swiper, and CSS-only modes</li>\n<li>Adjustable navigation with arrows, bullets, and progress bars</li>\n<li>Lightbox support for galleries</li>\n<li>Query Loop integration for post carousels</li>\n<li>Responsive item counts, spacing, and breakpoints</li>\n<li>Optional custom CSS and JavaScript controls</li>\n<li>A growing library of free, ready-to-customize templates</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Template Library</h3>\n<p>Choose from a growing collection of carousel templates directly in the block editor. Every template is included for free and is ready to customize.</p>\n<p>Templates that were previously presented as premium are now included for free. There are no premium-only templates, locked layouts, or paid upgrades. Open the Template Library from the carousel block or from the editor Command Palette and insert any available design without leaving the block editor.</p>\n<h3>External services</h3>\n<p>The Template Library retrieves its manifest, previews, and template content from the jsDelivr CDN (<code>cdn.jsdelivr.net</code>) when an authorized user opens or refreshes the library. Administrators can optionally enable a daily WP-Cron check for new and updated templates. Automatic checks are disabled until an administrator provides consent and can be disabled at any time from the Template Library.</p>\n<p>The plugin does not intentionally send WordPress content, user account details, or telemetry. Like any web request, jsDelivr receives standard connection data such as the site server IP address. See the <a href=\"https://www.jsdelivr.com/terms/privacy-policy-jsdelivr-net\" rel=\"nofollow ugc\">jsDelivr privacy policy</a>.</p>\n",
